audit claim checklist.\n39: \n40: ## RF-4 — the bounded mail poll: KEEP\n41: \n42: The executor kept a time-bounded 
poll on mail-catcher reads although delivery measured at 4 ms,\n43: and offered to remove it as speculative. **Ruling: 
keep it.** A live catcher is asynchronous by\n44: nature; a bounded poll is measurement robustness against real-world 
timing variance, not a\n45: speculative feature — and its comment records both the measurement and the reason for 
the\n46: bound, so the next reader is not misled about why it exists.\n47: \n48: ## RF-5 — no direct-rpc atomicity 
arm: RATIFIED, the ruled remedy stands\n49: \n50: The executor found the recorded live proof of mid-transaction 
