it produces a value the test then asserts on, so a suite can go green over it, which is\n * why `registry.ts` refuses 
one above the loop tier. A pending proxy answers NOTHING — it fakes no\n * behaviour, returns no value and can never 
produce a green. Its only possible effect is to turn one\n * id red, by name, with a detail the declaration machinery 
