minted\n9:  * by a simulator the test armed. That is the difference between the sim and this, and it is the only\n10:  
* difference this file claims.\n11:  *\n12:  * WHERE THE ENDPOINT COMES FROM. The slot's own `supabase status -o json` 
reports `MAILPIT_URL`, and\n13:  * the runner passes it into the child. It is NOT recomputed from `[local_smtp] port` 
plus the pool's\n14:  * per-slot port offset: that arithmetic is `db-pool.ts`'s, and a second copy of a rule is how 
two\n15:  * copies come to disagree while both look right (the warning `vendors.ts` states at its head).\n16:  *\n17:  
* WHY IT IS PROBED BEFORE IT IS GRANTED. A URL is a string. `capabilities.ts` grants `vendors.email`\n18:  * a `real` 
verdict on this value, so the grounds have to be positive: the catcher is asked what it\n19:  * is, and only an answer 
that identifies a catcher earns the grant. An unreachable endpoint refuses\n20:  * loudly here rather than turning 
into \"no confirmation email arrived\" three assertions later —\n21:  * which is the failure AI4DEV-59's own proof 
script called out and solved the same way.\n22:  *\n23:  * WHICH CATCHER. Measured rather than remembered, exactly as 
that transcript did it: the Supabase\n24:  * CLI has shipped Inbucket and, more recently, Mailpit, and their APIs 
differ. This item's\n25:  * verify-first record measured Mailpit v1.30.2 behind slot 1's port and the Inbucket shape 
answering\n26:  * 404. Both probes are still performed, so a CLI version that goes back is a named refusal 
instead\n27:  * of a mystery.\n28:  */\n29: \n30: import { attestationOf, stampAttestation, SLOT_ATTESTATION_BRAND, 
type LiveAttestation } from './capabilities.ts';\n31: \n32: export type LiveEmailMessage = {\n33:   /** the catcher's 
own id for the message */\n34:   id: string;\n35:   /** every recipient address the catcher recorded */\n36:   to: 
string[];\n37:   subject: string;\n38:   /** the message's text, as the catcher renders it — where a verification link 
