Vendors<Channel extends string = string> = {\n157:   email: EmailProviderSim<Channel>;\n158: };\n159: \n160: /* 
-------------------------------------------------------------- H4 semantic oracles */\n161: \n162: /**\n163:  * 
Judging the MEANING of generated text, where string-matching cannot decide.\n164:  *\n165:  * Three ratified 
acceptance criteria need this: AT-009.07 (rejection copy instructs and never\n166:  * accuses), AT-004.10 (Discovery 
output satisfies a fixture-specific semantic oracle), AT-033.07\n167:  * (the assistant's four framed answers, each 
with a pinned oracle). NONE of their suites exists\n168:  * yet, so what the ratified text pins today is not any 
finished rubric — it is the set of\n169:  * criterion KINDS the contract has to be able to express: semantic-absence, 
semantic-containment,\n170:  * count-minimum, numeric-tolerance, no-fabrication. That set is what the shapes below are 
