runs later),\n6:  *   - the tier contract (`AT_TIER` comes from the runner; there is NO default),\n7:  *   - the 
harness handshake: resolve the harness, build a world, tear both down per test.\n8:  *\n9:  * Two failure modes are 
kept strictly apart so a red is never ambiguous:\n10:  *   - `harness-missing` — AI4DEV-3's capability modules (H2-H6) 
are not in the tree.\n11:  *   - `sut-missing`     — the harness is up, but the requirement's implementation is 
not.\n12:  * Neither can produce a green. There is no skip, no `todo`, no swallowed assertion — a pending\n13:  * id 
fails loudly, stamped with its own AT id and the reason.\n14:  *\n15:  * ID BINDING: an id is supplied ONCE, at the 
`atTest` call site. The title, the failure stamp\n16:  * and the per-id report all derive from it. The bijection 
checker reads those call sites.\n17:  */\n18: \n19: import { appendFileSync, mkdirSync } from 'node:fs';\n20: import { 
