expected.length, applied: applied.length };\n953: }\n954: \n955: /* 
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- reset */\n956: \n957: /**\n958:  
* WHAT A PRE-DESTRUCTIVE IDENTITY READ PROVED (audit ruling B2, decision D13).\n959:  *\n960:  * The read itself lives 
beside the pool, because only the pool knows what a slot is. What travels\n961:  * from the read to the destructive 
act is this: the project id the CLI's own output POSITIVELY\n962:  * named, or `null` when the read proved no project 
at all.\n963:  */\n964: export interface SlotIdentityProof {\n965:   /** The project id the identity read proved, from 
