CLI so failures are catchable and bounded.\n972:  *\n973:  * WHY EVERY RUN: without it the second run works on the 
first run's leftover rows, and on a\n974:  * schema missing whatever migration landed since — a suite grading a 
database nobody established.\n975:  *\n976:  * A TARGET COSTS A PROOF, AND THE TYPE SYSTEM COLLECTS IT (audit ruling 
B2). D13 rules the identity\n977:  * read structurally ON the destructive path, \"never a separate call a caller can 
