FIX-phase rulings — AI4DEV-81 (per-item integration verification)\n2: \n3: Ruler: the FIX orchestrator sitting 
(fable). Subject: the judgments the executor raised in its\n4: FIX-AND-GOAL report (final code head 41bcadc, evidence 
commit f11eaa1). The executor proposed;\n5: the rulings are made here.\n6: \n7: ## RF-1 — the iteration count: THE CAP 
HELD\n8: \n9: The executor flagged that counting its baseline suite run as an attempt makes req-001 four\n10: cycles 
against the stated three. **Ruling: the baseline is measurement, not an attempt.** The\n11: draft phase deliberately 
never ran the verify suite, so the first run of it establishes the\n12: starting state — there is no fix in it to 
attempt. Three fix-and-verify cycles followed for\n13: req-001 and one for req-016, inside the three-attempt cap, and 
the greens moved monotonically\n14: with each cause traced to code. Flagging the ambiguity instead of absorbing it 
