nt-afec9a241af931aac\\loop\\items\\AI4DEV-81\\plan.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Plan — AI4DEV-81 
(per-item integration verification), batch with AI4DEV-45 (CI timeout counts queue time)\n2: \n3: Branch: 
`nirdrang/ai4dev-81-per-item-integration-verification-every-item-proves-its-ids`,\n4: cut from main at 466880d. 
Reserved database slot: **slot 1**, reserved under this item; it serves\n5: the pair. AI4DEV-45 is the batch partner: 
it rides this branch and pull request, and the pull\n6: request closes it with the one sanctioned closes-line.\n7: 
\n8: **AMENDED after gate 1** (11 findings, all accepted — one fixed differently; see\n9: `rulings-gate1.md` for each 
ruling with the reviewer's claim verbatim). This amended plan is\n10: what gets built.\n11: \n12: ## What the board 
items ask\n13: \n14: **AI4DEV-81** (primary): the goal step of every item runs the suite at BOTH tiers — loop\n15: 
(unchanged, CI's required check) and integration against the item's reserved slot — each graded\n16: per acceptance id 
with exact-match declarations. First concrete scope: migrate the live-proof\n17: checks of the three finished auth 
items (GitHub sign-in, email verification, sessions) into\n18: integration-mode test bodies. The live-proof script 
shrinks to vendor measurement only.\n19: Constraints: no new pool mechanics; the personal stack stays untouchable; 
CI's required check\n20: stays stub-based and fast; the requirement evidence gate is unchanged.\n21: \n22: 
**AI4DEV-45** (partner): raise the verify job's `timeout-minutes` from 15 into the 30–45 range,\n23: because the 
15-minute budget was consumed by runner queue time and killed the check before one\n24: step ran. The item states 
explicitly that the raise must NOT be justified by picking one of the\n25: two undistinguished stories (queue vs. dead 
runner).\n26: \n27: ## Facts established against the tree (evidence by pointer)\n28: \n29: - F1 — 
`.github/workflows/ci.yml` line 49 already carries `timeout-minutes: 30`, with a comment\n30:   recording the 
2026-08-06 queue deaths. `git log -L` shows the raise (15 → 30) landed in commit\n31:   2795926, the change that 
routed CI to a self-hosted runner behind a variable, merged as PR #44.\n32:   **The partner's remedy is already on 
main; it was never attributed to the partner item.**\n33: - F2 — `tests/at/harness/runner.ts` already implements the 
integration tier end to end: slot\n34:   occupancy via the item's reservation (`db-pool.ts occupy`), prepare (mirror, 
identity proof,\n35:   reset, migration-set proof), the evidence line, an allowlisted child environment carrying\n36:  
 `AT_SUPABASE_URL / _DB_URL / _ANON_KEY / _SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, and `--expect` at any tier.\n37: - F3 — 
`tests/at/harness/expected.ts` already supports per-tier declarations\n38:   (`tiers: { loop, integration, drill }`), 
with two declarable red kinds only:\n39:   `capability-pending` (exact capability names) and `pending` (phase). 
Bijection with the\n40:   requirement's P0 ids is enforced per tier.\n41: - F4 — `tests/at/expected/req-001.json` and 
`req-016.json` declare ONLY the loop tier today.\n42: - F5 — `tests/at/harness/registry.ts` (~line 619): above loop, 
the whole capability ledger must\n43:   contain zero stand-ins, enforced as a bare `expect(...).toEqual([])`. That 
failure detail fits\n44:   NEITHER declarable red kind — so today an integration run of any suite is undeclarable, 
not\n45:   merely red.\n46: - F6 — `tests/at/harness/capabilities.ts`: the witness table is CLOSED (six names); 
the\n47:   adapter-derived route (`fixtures.worlds`, every `sut.<key>`) stamps stand-in UNCONDITIONALLY;\n48:   
`clock.controlled`'s witness refuses any value without the freeze/advance seam, noting \"this\n49:   tree holds no 
attested real clock backing\". `oracles.judge` already returns real at\n50:   integration+live. `pendingCapability()` 
exists and throws `CapabilityPending` on any use.\n51: - F7 — `tests/at/suites/req-001/_fixture.ts` header: every 
`sut.<key>` from the loop adapter is a\n52:   stand-in, so \"nothing here can reach the integration-tier run\". The 
live evidence for the real\n53:   half lives in the three finished items' `proof-local.ts` transcripts (one machine's 
word, never\n54:   re-runnable): email verification checks (a, b, b2, d), sessions checks (a–e: sign-in row,\n55:   
refused sign-in adds no row, logout scope=local with a sibling-session control, expiry via a\n56:   transiently 
lowered `jwt_expiry` plus same-row refresh, password reset), and the signup set\n57:   (complete_signup atomicity 
leaving zero rows, the GitHub gate, the imported profile, database\n58:   backstops).\n59: - F8 — no OAuth app or 
credential exists for GitHub or Google in this environment. The provider\n60:   HANDSHAKES are unproved at every tier 
(fixture header, mirrors 4 and 5) and this item cannot\n61:   change that.\n62: - F9 — no Discovery send route exists 
in this repository; `sendDiscoveryMessage` is a stand-in\n63:   surface mirroring nothing (fixture header, closing 
paragraph).\n64: \n65: ## Decisions\n66: \n67: - **D1 — the goal step runs both tiers.** The executor's goal loop 
definition becomes: every\n68:   plan step at its done-criterion AND two exact-match results — `at:verify <req> --tier 
loop\n69:   --expect` for every declaration manifest (as CI's loop step discovers them), and `at:verify\n70:   <req> 
--tier integration --expect` for every declaration manifest, serially on the item's one\n71:   reserved slot. CI's 
BEHAVIOR is not changed by this item: the required check stays loop-only\n72:   and fast; the ONE edit 
`.github/workflows/ci.yml` receives is the comment neutralization of\n73:   ruling 11 (zero behavior change). Cost 
accepted at filing: a slot reset plus a real run per\n74:   manifest, minutes per item.\n75: - **D2 — the integration 
refusal becomes declarable (amended, rulings 3 and 5).** The registry's\n76:   above-loop stand-in gate (F5) stops 
being a bare expect and throws `CapabilityPending` naming\n77:   the stubbed capability names, so an id whose harness 
assembly still leans on LEDGER stand-ins\n78:   is a red of exactly the declarable `capability-pending` shape. The 
METHOD axis is covered at\n79:   use time instead: callable pending proxies (D3) throw `CapabilityPending` naming\n80: 
  `sut.accounts.<method>` on use, so an id leaning on an unbacked method is declarably red\n81:   without failing the 
whole suite. Strictness is preserved: reds stay red, names are exact, the\n82:   declaration machinery refuses drift. 
For any integration GREEN to exist, ledger construction\n83:   itself becomes tier-aware (D4): at integration it 
constructs the attested real clock, the live\n84:   mail-catcher email capability, and live-route fixtures/sut entries 
— a stand-in-free ledger on\n85:   positive evidence, never by relaxing the gate.\n86: - **D3 — the loader selects the 
adapter by tier (amended, rulings 2 and 5).** Loop keeps\n87:   `_fixture.ts` unchanged. Integration loads a 
suite-provided live adapter module (new file\n88:   beside the fixture, its own factory signature — no 
`ControlledClock` parameter) that backs a\n89:   closed, exported ENUMERATION of `sut.accounts` METHOD names against 
the slot's stack, and\n90:   supplies callable pending proxies for every method it does not back. Admission checks: 
every\n91:   enumerated name must exist on the loaded adapter surface; every `real` grant carries D4's\n92:   
attestation evidence; nothing is ever granted `real` by prefix. The `sut.accounts` ledger\n93:   entry is `real` with 
evidence naming the backed enumeration and the attestation; a pending\n94:   proxy can only ever refuse, so the 
failure direction stays false-red. A suite with no live\n95:   adapter module assembles with the loop fixture and is 
caught by D2's gate — all ids declarably\n96:   red.\n97: - **D4 — real provenance only on positive evidence (amended, 
rulings 1, 3, 4).** Shape checks\n98:   (`localStackProblems`) remain a guard, never grounds. Positive grounds = a 
live round-trip\n99:   binding: `prepare()` mints a per-run attestation nonce and writes it into the slot 
database\n100:   after the reset; the child receives `AT_SLOT_ATTESTATION`; live construction reads the nonce\n101:   
back THROUGH the supplied coordinates and refuses on mismatch or read failure. The clock: at\n102:   integration the 
harness constructs an attested real clock with NO control seam; the\n103:   `clock.controlled` witness gains the 
attested-real branch its refusal text anticipates,\n104:   granted only on the harness's own real-clock constructor's 
attestation. Email: at integration\n105:   the ledger constructs a live email capability reading the slot stack's mail 
catcher (endpoint\n106:   derived from the slot's own status/config, attested, probed before grant); the sim branch 
of\n107:   the witness is untouched. The witness table stays closed; the live route is a separate\n108:   constructor 
with its own admission partition; the failure direction of any fabrication stays\n109:   false-red, never 
false-green.\n110: - **D5 — per-tier test bodies are permitted, one body per id per tier (amended, ruling 4).**\n111:  
 The item's own words are \"integration-mode test bodies\". Some live checks are different\n112:   procedures proving 
the same criterion, so `atTest` gains an explicit per-tier body form. The\n113:   per-tier CONTEXT TYPES carry the 
capability differences: an integration body's clock type\n114:   exposes no `freezeAt`/`advance`, so seam misuse fails 
typecheck. The invariant the runner\n115:   already enforces — exactly one registration and one vitest result per id 
per run — holds at\n116:   every tier. A criterion's meaning never forks: both bodies cite the same acceptance 
text.\n117: - **D6 — the integration floor is the three migrated CHECK SETS; per-id green follows the full\n118:   
criterion (amended, rulings 7 and 9).** The item's done-criterion mandates migrating the three\n119:   finished items' 
live checks; it does not license any green the migrated checks do not prove.\n120:   An id is declared green ONLY 
where its integration body proves the criterion's full text\n121:   against the live stack (see the table's conditions 
for .01, .09, .13); every other req-001 id\n122:   is declared red with its exact kind. Provider-handshake ids (F8) 
and the Discovery floor id\n123:   (F9) are NOT declared green at integration — a green that needs a credential nobody 
holds or a\n124:   route nobody built would be the false green this repository exists to kill.\n125: - **D7 — req-016 
gets an integration declaration too** (all ids red, exact kinds, via D2), so\n126:   the goal step's discovery loop 
over every manifest runs exact-match at both tiers with nothing\n127:   skipped.\n128: - **D8 — the live-proof script 
is demoted in the process text.** The goal step's verification\n129:   instrument is `at:verify` alone; a one-off 
proof script is legitimate only as a vendor\n130:   measurement feeding a plan decision. The three committed 
transcripts stay in the record as\n131:   history; nothing is deleted.\n132: - **D9 — integration joins the merge 
evidence.** The merge ruling states both exact-match\n133:   results (tier, requirement, exit, slot evidence line) 
pinned to the head. Process files:\n134:   `WORKFLOW.md` (goal step and merge ruling lines), `executor.md` (goal 
definition),\n135:   `orchestrator.md` + `orchestrator-opus.md` (merge ruling content — the twins are edited 
both\n136:   or neither; `loop/work/twin-check.ps1` is the check).\n137: - **D10 — the partner needs one comment edit, 
no behavior change (amended, ruling 11).** By F1\n138:   the remedy is applied, inside the item's 30–45 range, with 
the runaway bound kept. The\n139:   existing workflow comment WAS found to elect the queue story (`ci.yml:46` asserts 
\"hosted\n140:   capacity queued this job\"), which the partner item forbids; the comment is amended to state\n141:   
both candidate explanations as undistinguished — no runner for 11-15 minutes, hosted queueing\n142:   and a dead 
runner lane equally consistent with the evidence, the budget expired before a\n143:   single step ran. This pull 
request closes the partner with the sanctioned closes-line; the\n144:   merge ruling declares that line and records F1 
plus the amended comment as the partner's\n145:   evidence. Nothing else in the tree is touched for it.\n146: - **D11 
— slicing: yes.** The diff is large enough that one review would be a wall. The code\n147:   gate runs per slice: 
**slice 1** — harness machinery (D2, D3's loader, D4, D5's registration\n148:   form, D12's config transform, 
selftests); **slice 2** — the live adapter, the migrated\n149:   integration bodies, both declaration manifests, the 
ci.yml comment neutralization (D10), and\n150:   the process-text changes (D1, D8, D9).\n151: - **D12 — standing low 
`jwt_expiry` in the generated slot config (new, ruling 6).** There is no\n152:   transient config override and no 
restoration to prove. `generateSlotConfig`\n153:   (`tests/at/harness/db-pool.ts:308`) gains one sanctioned, pinned 
transform: slot configs set a\n154:   standing low `auth.jwt_expiry` (target ~120 s; exact value settled by step 5's 
verify-first).\n155:   The value rides the existing generated-config + hash-marker + restart machinery — applied 
when\n156:   absent, never restored, identical every run. No test body edits config or restarts the slot,\n157:   
ever. This makes AT-001.12's expiry arm and AT-001.13's client auto-refresh provable inside\n158:   the single 
manifest run. The generator's selftests assert the transform is the only new\n159:   difference it produces.\n160: 
\n161: ## Steps, each with its done-criterion\n162: \n163: 1. **Confirm the id ↔ check-set mapping** against the 
acceptance file\n164:    (`.taskmaster/docs/acceptance/at-req-001.md`) and the three proof transcripts; amend 
the\n165:    table below from \"target\" to \"settled\" per id. Done: every one of req-001's 37 P0 ids has a\n166:    
settled integration disposition recorded in the amended plan, each green citing the check(s)\n167:    that prove it 
live-provable.\n168: 2. **Registry: declarable above-loop refusal (D2).** Done: a harness selftest proves 
`open()`\n169:    above loop with stand-ins on the LEDGER throws `CapabilityPending` naming the exact stubbed\n170:    
names; a selftest proves a callable pending proxy throws `CapabilityPending` naming\n171:    `sut.accounts.<method>` 
on use; every existing selftest and the loop-tier `--expect` runs for\n172:    req-001 and req-016 stay green.\n173: 
3. **Capabilities: the live-evidence route, the attestation binding, the attested real clock,\n174:    and the live 
email branch (D4).** Done: selftests prove (a) real provenance requires the\n175:    attestation round-trip — granted 
with a nonce read back through the supplied coordinates,\n176:    refused for personal-stack ports, hosted-reference 
keys, absent evidence, AND\n177:    well-formed-but-fabricated coordinates whose database does not hold this run's 
nonce (ruling\n178:    1's case); (b) the closed witness table still refuses unknown names AND the new live 
route\n179:    refuses unknown and unenumerated names — nothing is granted `real` by prefix (ruling 2);\n180:    (c) 
the attested-real clock branch grants only on the harness's own constructor attestation\n181:    and the live email 
