\n251: ### AT-001.02, AT-001.03, AT-001.10 — no confirmation asked for, and none needed\n252: \n253: The plan settles 
these red on F8 (no OAuth credential exists) and F9 (no Discovery route exists in\n254: this repository). Both facts 
were re-checked and both hold: `supabase/functions/` contains exactly\n255: `complete-signup` and 
`create-organization`, and 58 (f2) records the absent GitHub credential.\n256: \n257: ---\n258: \n259: ## Part C — the 
GATE-2 verify-first question (ruling S2-3)\n260: \n261: Written by the FIX executor. Appended; nothing above is 
changed.\n262: \n263: ### The question the ruling asks\n264: \n265: > \"the executor inspects the deployed 
complete-signup function. If an input exists that passes\n266: > upfront validation and fails inside the transaction 
after earlier writes, the arm drives that\n267: > input and asserts zero rows.\"\n268: \n269: ### ANSWER: NO. No such 
input exists on the deployed surface. The remedy takes the second branch\n270: \n271: The only write inside 
`public.complete_signup` that can fail AFTER an earlier write has succeeded is\n272: the LAST one — the acknowledgment 
insert — and every input that would make it fail is refused by the\n273: deployed function's own upfront validation, 
before the database is called at all.\n274: \n275: ### Evidence 1 — where the function can fail, read from the 
source\n276: \n277: `supabase/migrations/20260809090000_volunteer_github_link_and_imported_profile.sql` 
recreates\n278: `public.complete_signup`. Its body is in two halves:\n279: \n280: 1. **Every argument check comes 
first, before the first insert** — the `platform_admin` refusal, the\n281:    unknown-type refusal, the NGO 
organisation-name rule, the volunteer organisation-name rule, and\n282:    the whole volunteer block (the linked 
handle, the identity backstop, the four import checks). A\n283:    refusal from any of them happens with ZERO rows 
written, so it proves a refusal and not a\n284:    rollback.\n285: 2. **Then the four writes**: the account (1), the 
organisation and membership for an NGO (2, 3), the\n286:    volunteer profile (3b), and the acknowledgment (4) 
last.\n287: \n288: The account insert's own failure mode is the `unique_violation` of a second completion — the 
FIRST\n289: write, with nothing before it to roll back. Every other table-level constraint on the path\n290: 
(`organizations.name`, and the four on `volunteer_profiles`) is pre-checked by the function body with\n291: the SAME 
predicate the constraint carries, so the insert cannot be the thing that fails. The\n292: migration says as much in 
its own words at the acknowledgment insert: \"IT STAYS LAST, and that\n293: placement is depended upon: the atomicity 
proof makes this write fail after the earlier ones have\n294: succeeded.\"\n295: \n296: So the ONE lever is 
`acknowledgments.text_version`, whose constraint is\n297: `check (length(btrim(text_version)) > 0)`.\n298: \n299: ### 
Evidence 2 — the deployed function's upfront validation, MEASURED\n300: \n301: `validateCompleteSignup` 
(`supabase/functions/_shared/accounts.ts`) was driven with `bun` over every\n302: candidate lever. Output, 
verbatim:\n303: \n304: ```\n305: REFUSED   ngo, acknowledgmentTextVersion ''  ->  the ToS + Platform Promise 
acknowledgment text version is required …\n306: REFUSED   ngo, ack version single space  ->  the ToS + Platform 
Promise acknowledgment text version is required …\n307: REFUSED   ngo, ack version tab  ->  the ToS + Platform Promise 
acknowledgment text version is required …\n308: REFUSED   ngo, ack version NBSP U+00A0  ->  the ToS + Platform Promise 
acknowledgment text version is required …\n309: ACCEPTED  ngo, ack version ZWSP U+200B  ->  accountType=ngo 
organizationName=\"X\" ackVersion=\"<U+200B>\" githubHandle=null\n310: REFUSED   ngo, ack version omitted  ->  the ToS 
+ Platform Promise acknowledgment text version is required …\n311: REFUSED   ngo, organizationName tab  ->  an NGO 
signup must carry a non-empty organisation name\n312: REFUSED   ngo, organizationName NBSP  ->  an NGO signup must 
carry a non-empty organisation name\n313: ACCEPTED  ngo, organizationName ZWSP  ->  accountType=ngo 
organizationName=\"<U+200B>\" ackVersion=\"v1\" githubHandle=null\n314: REFUSED   volunteer, handle of tabs  ->  a 
volunteer signup cannot be completed without a linked GitHub account …\n315: ```\n316: \n317: ### Evidence 3 — what a 
REAL Postgres says about the two values that pass\n318: \n319: The one accepted candidate is the zero-width space, so 
the question is whether the constraint refuses\n320: it. Asked of slot 1's own running database, read-only:\n321: 
\n322: ```\n323: 
{\"zwsp_len\":1,\"tab_len\":1,\"space_len\":0,\"zwsp_not_blank_regex\":true,\"tab_not_blank_regex\":false}\n324: 
```\n325: \n326: `btrim` with no second argument strips THE SPACE CHARACTER ONLY. So\n327: `length(btrim(<U+200B>)) = 
1 > 0` — the acknowledgment insert SUCCEEDS on the one input the validator\n328: lets through. The same holds for the 
organisation name.\n329: \n330: ### Why that closes the question rather than merely failing to open it\n331: \n332: 
