four plausible strings.\n60:  *\n61:  * So a live capability carries an ATTESTATION: an object the harness's own live 
constructors stamp\n62:  * onto the value AFTER a round trip that could only have succeeded against the prepared slot. 
The\n63:  * round trip is `attestation.ts`'s — `prepare()` mints a nonce, writes it into the slot database\n64:  * 
after the reset, and the child reads it back THROUGH the coordinates it was handed. \"These\n65:  * coordinates 
answered with this run's runner-minted value\" is the grounds; nothing weaker is.\n66:  *\n67:  * WHAT THIS FILE CAN 
AND CANNOT CHECK, said exactly, because a closure claim wider than the truth is\n68:  * the defect this file exists to 
remove. It has no I/O and performs no round trip. It checks that a\n69:  * value carries a well-formed attestation 
