named a body for a DIFFERENT tier and no default — which\n790:  * `tierBodyProblem` refuses before this is ever 
consulted in the real path. It is returned rather\n791:  * than thrown so the selftest can state the rule positively: 
a body written for one tier does not\n792:  * run at another.\n793:  */\n794: export function 
chooseTierBody<B>(bodies: Record<string, B | undefined>, tier: Tier | null): B | null {\n795:   const named = tier === 
null ? undefined : bodies[tier];\n796:   return named ?? bodies.default ?? bodies.loop ?? null;\n797: }\n798: \n799: 
